/* book exam traps: On a flyback the primary-to-secondary turns ratio n = N1/N2 sits in the denominator of the CCM gain. Vo = Vs·D·(N2/N1) is the forward formula, not the flyback formula. | Forgetting the leakage spike: Vs + n·Vo is only the ideal switch stress. The RCD clamp handles the extra spike, and the device rating must leave margin. | A forward converter with a 1:1 reset winding must keep D below 0.5. Pushing D higher leaves no time to reset the core, so flux walks and the core saturates. | Do not treat the flyback transformer as a true transformer in the energy-transfer sense. It is a coupled inductor; the primary inductance is the energy-storing element. | Duty ratio D is a fraction, not a percentage. Enter 0.4 into the formulas, not 40. */
